On Mar 26, 5:10 pm, "3cnf...@gmail.com" <3cnf...@gmail.com> wrote:
> All right, my Monk has been *incredibly* lucky. He found a wand of
> wishing on  dlvl 2 and an (uncursed) magic lamp and coaligned altar in
> the Gnomish mines. He's currently standing in the coaligned temple in
> Minetown
> at Exp 5, figuring out what to wish for. But he's a *monk* and doesn't
> want to wish for body armor.and his OTHER wish ideas (already has 2
> blessed charging scrolls) are:

You want MR and reflection as soon as possible, and it's very hard to
get both for a monk (especially if you want to keep the robe and not
wear a shield--monks make good casters).


> 1. An artifact. Monks have poor AC, and the quest boss is tough, hence
> he wants an early advantage.
>         Staff of Aesculpacus: My characters often end up with underpowered
> weapons, and the Drain Life ability would sure help with Master Kaen. However,
> I might be able

Not a total waste because of the regen, but weapons usually aren't
worthwile.  I wouldn't, but I could see a case for it.

>         Orb of Fate: 1/2 physical damage and magic resistance, would help me
> be less wimpy. But it's FRIGGIN HEAVY.

Does NOT grant magic resistance.  Does give 1/2 magic damage, which
doesn't help against, say, wands of death/touch of death/polytraps/
etc.

>         Eye of the Aetheopica: The best escape item. If I were at Exp 10, I'd
> probably wish for it right away thanks to the branchport ability, but I'm so
> wimpy that this item could kill me when
>         I invoke it and I'm in trouble. Also, the only spell I know is
> "sleep", so the spellcasting boost isn't so great.

The Eye should be wish #1.  It would probably be the best artifact in
the game even without granting MR; with it, it's ridiculously awesome.

You will take at most 20 hp damage when invoking it, so keep that in
mind.

I don't get your last sentence; sleep is incredibly powerful and being
able to spam it is a big boost to survivability.

> 2. ring of slow digestion so I don't starve. (since I can ID this from
> sinks, will probably wait until actually starving)

Only useful in the very early game, unless you're trying to stay
vegetarian when it's useful a bit longer.  Remember that the alignment
hit for eating meat is pretty laughable for a non-pacifist, and stay
well-fed.

By Sokoban it's pretty much worthless either way, but if you need it
to survive until then it might be worth it.

Conflict, telecontrol, and levitation are the only rings that might
merit a wish at some point, or maybe free action if you're drowning in
wishes by the Sanctum.  Conflict is the only one that you might
consider now (or soon), but I'd wait on it.  Esp. with a monk.

> 3. amulet of reflection, because there's a big bones pile on the first
> floor of minetown (dove into hole instead of looting it) and the pile may have
> contained nasty attack wands.

That could be worth it.

> 4. 5000 gold pieces so I can get some divine protection. After all,
> only at Exp 5 right now.

I'd rather go for, say, +3 jumping boots, or some other more
constructive immediate AC boost--you'll get divine protection soon
enough (you should be able to get the 1st purchase now if you loot the
stores) and in the interim I'd rather have jumping than a couple AC.
And once you get the protection anyway, you'll still have your cool
item.

And, with the marker(s) that you will wish up you now have a permanent
keeper item to enchant up to +4/5

> 5. magic marker

If you know ?enchant armor, at least one is an absolute "right now"
item.

> 6. Wait on wishes until finishing sokoban/emergency - would wish for
> Amulet of Life Saving in a true
> emergency. I'm quite reluctant to do this because my charging scrolls
> could catch fire (no bag).

Put the charging scrolls in a chest somewhere.

> I already have a tinning kit courtesy of the minetown shops, so trolls
> shouldn't pose a problem.
> My main priority is to survive until the Castle. I *don't want a YASD
> after getting this lucky*.

I'd go for MR (Eye!), reflection, and markers--especially if you know ?
enchant armor.  I'll usually go for 2 blessed and 1 cursed marker with
the castle wand, maybe less if I've found one and/or been really lucky
with my scroll finds.

At this point, I might even wish for ?ea and a marker; enchant up the
keeper items first, but I'd be more than willing to enchant up a small
shield, leather helm/gloves, etc to get the AC.  They're all
reasonably decent final items anyway, and you have a chance to get
another marker at the Castle to enchant up your rounded-out ascension
kit.




